A||N||5||grinthock||Runs Bad In Wet||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||06-01-2001||09:34 PM||||Anyone elses car idle kinda crappy in the wet?  Mine idles FINE when it's dry out but when it's wet I sit at lights and it dips below 500rpm, struggling to stay alive, then she jumps to 1200... ONLY in the wet<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://grinthock.2y.net/pics/87gt/S_P000386.JPG">  <P>Home page: <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com<BR>Home" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroworld.com<BR>Home</A>  of the fiero voting booth!<BR>Owner of 85 GT<BR>87 GT Silver<BR>1995 Ford Escort Wagoon POS||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrFeeArrow||06-01-2001||09:49 PM||||My 2M4 had the same problem,....I repalced all the wires/distributor cap and coil. I also put a good bead of blue RTV around the base of the Distributor cap just to make sure moisture stayed out.<P>I had a 1972 Super Beatle back in the 70's that was notorious for this up North,....I always carried a can of wd40 with me to displace any moisture when the bug would DIE! It worked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||06-01-2001||11:15 PM||||stop getting your car excited, it wouldn't get wet<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||06-02-2001||05:47 PM||||I thought cars were supposed to run a little bit better when the air was a little humid and thick.  The extra density of the air would hold more fuel.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-02-2001||06:44 PM||||You'll have to go thru the engine bay and clean everything for a start. Dirt holds water... This alone can be trouble.<P>Once the bay is clean. Your most likely suspects are ignition parts/wires wet. Followed by wet sensor connections and charging system.<P>One thing to do is go over all connectors and clean them. Work a little dielectric into connectors that may not be sealing like they should.||||reg||1
Z||000005||poupas||06-04-2001||05:04 PM||||I have had that problem on my old fiero and also on a celica. It is usually your wires that are the problem. Like the other member said you should change all your wires etc... .In the meantime keep that WD40 with you at all times and if it rains and your car dies, spray it over your wires, and you have a fix, until the next rainfall at least. ||||reg||1
